@jyz0309 The details of the metric we'd like to record are laid out in the KEP here: https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/blob/master/keps/sig-auth/2579-psp-replacement/README.md#monitoring

Most of the implementation should go in the `pod-security-admission.k8s.io/metrics` package (currently a placeholder: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/pod-security-admission/metrics/metrics.go).

The `RecordEvaluation` interface should probably be called from the main admission.Validate method: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/staging/src/k8s.io/pod-security-admission/admission/admission.go#L204

I think it probably makes sense to update the interface method to take the admission attributes, and the AdmissionResponse, and then put all the logic about whether & how to record a given request behind the admission interface. In other words, something like this:

```go
type EvaluationRecorder interface {
	RecordEvaluation(attrs admission.Attributes, response *admissionv1.AdmissionResponse)
}

type PrometheusRecorder struct {
  // ...
}

func NewPrometheusRecorder(/* ... */) {
  // ...
}
```

One caveat: using `admission.Attributes` will result in a circular dependency. You can either move the existing attributes interface to the API package, or create a `metrics.Attributes` interface with the relevant subset of the admission attributes. I could be convinced by either approach.

